---
const title = 'Sciweon - Data Infrastructure for AI Agents';
const description = 'Cross-industry scientific data and evidence infrastructure for AI agents, starting with drug discovery. Built so agents get facts with provenance, not guesses.';
const canonical = 'https://sciweon.com/';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0a0a" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
  <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Structured, agent-ready scientific data and evidence for AI agents." />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <header>
      <h1>Sciweon</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Data infrastructure for AI agents</p>
      <p class="lede">Structured, agent-ready scientific data and evidence. Records carry their source and, where recorded, a confidence score - so an agent can check a claim instead of taking it on trust.</p>
    </header>
    <section>
      <h2>Domains</h2>
      <div class="domains">
        <article class="domain">
          <h3>Drug Discovery <span class="badge badge-alpha">Alpha</span></h3>
          <p>Compounds, bioactivity, clinical trials, regulatory signals, and prior-failure records. For agents doing virtual lab work before any wet experiment.</p>
          <a class="link" href="mailto:hello@sciweon.com">Request access</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Design principles</h2>
      <ul class="principles">
        <li><strong>Agent-first</strong> Designed for machines to consume directly. No human search-UX overhead in the data layer.</li>
        <li><strong>Cross-source</strong> Same fact verified across independent providers. Disagreement is captured, not hidden.</li>
        <li><strong>Provenance</strong> Records carry the source, timestamp and extraction method they were built from, so a claim can be traced back.</li>
        <li><strong>Confidence recorded</strong> Where a confidence score is computed it is returned rather than hidden. It is a recorded score, not a guarantee of correctness.</li>
        <li><strong>Negative evidence</strong> Failed trials, retractions, withdrawn drugs, post-market signals - collected as first-class data.</li>
        <li><strong>Dated snapshots</strong> Evidence responses report the snapshot date they were served from, so an answer can be pinned to a point in time. No refresh cadence is promised.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>For AI agents</h2>
      <p>Sciweon is not a search engine for humans. The intended user is an AI agent doing real research work - selecting compound leads, scoring trial designs, and avoiding prior-failure repeats.</p>
      <p>API and MCP server are in private alpha. No public release date is published. To get on the alpha list: <a href="mailto:hello@sciweon.com">hello@sciweon.com</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer>
    Sciweon - Data infrastructure for AI agents.<br />
    Drug Discovery alpha. No public release date is published.
  </footer>
</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    color: #e0e0e0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    line-height: 1.6;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  main {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 5rem;
    flex: 1 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
  }
  header { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: #fff; }
  .tagline { font-size: 1.1rem; color: #8b8b8b; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: #c8c8c8; max-width: 640px; margin: 0; }
  section { margin-top: 3rem; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: #6b8aff;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .domains {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .domain {
    background: #111;
    border: 1px solid #1f1f1f;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .domain h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .badge {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .badge-live { background: #0f3a1f; color: #4ade80; }
  .badge-alpha { background: #3a2c0f; color: #fbbf24; }
  .badge-planned { background: #2a2a2a; color: #888; }
  .domain p { color: #a0a0a0; font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; flex: 1; }
  .domain .link { color: #6b8aff; font-size: 0.88rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .domain .link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .principles { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .principles li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1f1f1f;
    color: #c8c8c8;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .principles li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .principles strong {
    color: #6b8aff;
    font-weight: 600;
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 9rem;
  }
  a { color: #6b8aff; text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  footer {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #1f1f1f;
    color: #555;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    h1 { font-size: 1.85rem; }
    main { padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
  }
</style>
